sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: docs/reference/tasks.md#complete-and-cleanup. Orchestrator 2026-11-08: keeping approved work is a precondition of completion, not a step of it; removal never wakes a task VM; the release refuses a VM that resumes.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: task:complete
  %% kind: tasks.complete
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>repository · PRs
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Incus over ssh
  CLI->>GW: task:complete 42
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit task:complete 42 --yes`
  %%> - syntax: `[task] [--yes] [--json]`
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the group is `settling` or `waiting_for_review`, or `running` or `reviewing` with a watched pull request that merged or closed; a `completed` group retries its removal
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Gateway
  GW->>GH: Compare the task branch<br/>approved...task-42
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - resolves the group's latest approved commit: the latest commit Orbit reviewed (ADR 0203), or else the commit of the latest approval
  %%> - reads origin's task branch head and compares it with that commit, with a `contents: read` token
  %%> - only when GitHub answers that the branch does not exist (404) and the group's pull request merged does that pull request's head stand in; the pull request is read with a `pull_requests: read` token
  %%> - skipped when the group has no approval, or holds no workspace and no task VM
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the release deletes the VM, and a commit that only the VM holds would go with it
  GH-->>GW: Branch reaches it
  %%> Result:
  %%> - otherwise completion refuses with HTTP 409 `tasks.approved_work_unpublished`, names the commit and the branch, and changes nothing: run `task:publish` first, which resumes a parked VM
  %%> - every other outcome refuses the same way: a GitHub read that fails, a branch that is gone without a merged pull request
  Note over GW: Complete the group<br/>stop work · subtasks cancelled
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - stores how the watched pull request ended, stops the running implementer, reviewer and checks, and marks the group `completed`
  %%> - runs the Project teardown in the guest and copies the agent transcripts, only while the VM is `ready`; a parked VM is never started
  Note over GW: Admit the release<br/>VM row locked · re-read
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - no other Operation is open on the VM: a resume that boots it refuses the release with HTTP 409 `operation.target_busy`; the group still completes and asks for `removal_failure` assistance, and a later complete retries
  %%> - an open release is reused, so a repeated complete admits no second one
  GW->>SW: Start the release<br/>operation-task-vm-slot-release
  SW->>H: Delete the VM<br/>and its seed clone
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the release of docs/cli/task/vm-release.mmd: the VM, its seed clone, its identity volume and its hub peer go
  SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>slot free
  Note over GW: Delete the Node record<br/>Instance · group unbound
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the Node and the workspace Instance go, and the group no longer names the workspace
